{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-diameter","title":"lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-diameter","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.md","line":376,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex#lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-diameter","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex","label":"lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-diameter","line":890,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Bonnet--Synge index inequality]\n  \\label{lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-diameter}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0266}\n  \\uses{rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases, def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds, %\n    lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core}\n\n  \\dcref{ch6:6.3.1}\n  If $(M,g)$ satisfies $\\sec\\ge k>0$, then geodesics of length $>\\pi/\\sqrt k$\n  cannot be locally minimizing.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases,lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core}\n  \\sketch\n  Use \\(V(t)=\\sin(\\pi t/l)E(t)\\) in the proper second-variation formula. The preceding scalar inequality makes the second variation negative when \\(l>\\pi/\\sqrt{k}\\), so the geodesic is not minimizing.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Bonnet--Synge index inequality] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7065742d6368362d626f6e6e65742d73796e67652d6469616d65746572\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0266</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23rem%3Apet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases\">↗ rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23def%3Apet-ch6-sec-bounds\">↗ def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23lem%3Apet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core\">↗ lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch6:6.3.1</span></span>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> satisfies <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\sec \\ge k&gt;0$\">$\\sec \\ge k&gt;0$</span>, then geodesics of length <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$&gt;\\pi /\\sqrt k$\">$&gt;\\pi /\\sqrt k$</span> cannot be locally minimizing.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23rem%3Apet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases\">↗ rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23lem%3Apet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core\">↗ lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core</a> \\sketch Use <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$V(t)=\\sin (\\pi t/l)E(t)$\">$V(t)=\\sin (\\pi t/l)E(t)$</span> in the proper second-variation formula. The preceding scalar inequality makes the second variation negative when <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$l&gt;\\pi /\\sqrt{k}$\">$l&gt;\\pi /\\sqrt{k}$</span>, so the geodesic is not minimizing. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-diameter","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases","title":"rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases","label":"rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds","title":"def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds","label":"def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core","title":"lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core","label":"lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-diameter","title":"cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-diameter","label":"cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-diameter"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem","label":"thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-diameter","title":"lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-diameter","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[Bonnet--Synge index inequality]\n  \\label{lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-diameter}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0266}\n  \\uses{rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases, def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds, %\n    lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core}\n\n  \\dcref{ch6:6.3.1}\n  If $(M,g)$ satisfies $\\sec\\ge k>0$, then geodesics of length $>\\pi/\\sqrt k$\n  cannot be locally minimizing.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases,lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core}\n  \\sketch\n  Use \\(V(t)=\\sin(\\pi t/l)E(t)\\) in the proper second-variation formula. The preceding scalar inequality makes the second variation negative when \\(l>\\pi/\\sqrt{k}\\), so the geodesic is not minimizing.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases","title":"rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds","title":"def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core","title":"lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}